{
  "id": "grammar.a1.01.02.ser",
  "title": "Soy: saying who you are",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Soy",
      "content": "Soy is the first-person singular form of ser, meaning “to be”. Use soy to identify yourself or say who you are. A simple introduction is Soy + name."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Ser: first person",
      "rows": [
        [
          "yo soy",
          "I am"
        ],
        [
          "soy Carlos",
          "I am Carlos"
        ],
        [
          "soy Meg",
          "I am Meg"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Soy Carlos.",
          "english": "I am Carlos."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Soy Meg.",
          "english": "I am Meg."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Soy Ana.",
          "english": "I am Ana."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Spanish often leaves out the subject pronoun yo because the verb form already identifies the speaker. For now, focus on the useful pattern Soy + name."
    }
  ]
}
